Developer Certificate of Origin (lightweight)
=============================================

Clawix uses the same lightweight sign-off model as ClawJS.

By adding a `Signed-off-by: Name <email>` line to a commit, you certify that:

1. You wrote the contribution, or you have the right to submit it under the
   repository license.
2. You understand that the contribution and your sign-off may be public.
3. You are not knowingly submitting material that violates someone else's
   rights.
4. You agree that the contribution may be distributed under the license used by
   the files you changed.

Example:

```
Signed-off-by: Ada Lovelace <ada@example.com>
```

This DCO is intended to keep contribution provenance lightweight. It is not a
Contributor License Agreement.
